des its final day; without a date it remains until explicitly ended. Forecasts, missing-start hints and cycle reminders stop, while a neutral status shows the reason and end. New observed bleeding is saved, but the pause ends only if you separately confirm it as a new period. Keep pause or cancelling that question preserves both the bleeding record and the pause. Ending the pause manually resumes planning today without creating a bleeding entry.</p><p>After resumption, only entries from the resumption day, or after the scheduled end, form the new history. Three new starts are needed; old cycles do not produce an overdue warning. Confirm bleeding as a new period only if that is how it has been identified. Bleeding during pregnancy needs prompt medical advice; bleeding after menopause also needs medical assessment. Ending a planning pause does not establish that a pregnancy or menopause has ended.</p>"
