diff --git a/magnolie-organizer-windows/app/web/stil.css b/magnolie-organizer-windows/app/web/stil.css
index 6b044395f143ed1d7dba9010370d852f4bede1f0..d58fdc9ccbf211bc7217f68d2194f12fe6d74339 100644
--- a/magnolie-organizer-windows/app/web/stil.css
+++ b/magnolie-organizer-windows/app/web/stil.css
@@ -6507,3 +6507,33 @@ body[data-linien="aus"] #tb-notiz {
 .kontakt-quelle-gespeichert { border-color: #b86600; background: rgba(230, 126, 0, .12); }
 .kontakt-quelle-eingang { border-color: #23834a; background: rgba(35, 131, 74, .12); }
 @media (max-width: 620px) { .kontakt-quellenspalten { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
+
+/* Optional cycle estimates are derived display, never recorded bleeding. */
+.zyklus-prognose-kasten {
+  flex: 0 0 auto;
+  max-height: 24vh;
+  overflow-y: auto;
+  margin: 8px;
+  padding: 10px 12px;
+  border: 1px dashed var(--linie-stark);
+  border-radius: 6px;
+  color: inherit;
+  background: var(--papier);
+  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
+  font-size: .9em;
+}
+.zyklus-prognose-kasten h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 1.05em; }
+.zyklus-prognose-kasten p { margin: 5px 0; line-height: 1.35; }
+.zyklus-prognose-datum { font-weight: 700; }
+.zyklus-prognose-hinweis { border-inline-start: 3px solid currentColor; padding-inline-start: 8px; }
+.zyklus-prognose-details summary { cursor: pointer; padding-block: 4px; }
+.zyklus-prognose-details summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 2px; }
+
+.zyklus-prognose-marke { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 3px; border: 1px solid transparent; background: transparent; color: #983851; border-radius: 3px; padding: 1px 3px; font: inherit; font-weight: 700; }
+button.zyklus-prognose-marke { cursor: pointer; }
+.zyklus-prognose-marke:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 1px; }
+.zyklus-prognose-tropfen { width: 14px; height: 18px; flex: 0 0 auto; }
+.zyklus-bestaetigung-schleier { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 180; display: grid; place-items: center; padding: 16px; background: #0007; }
+.zyklus-bestaetigung-dialog { width: min(480px, 100%); max-height: 85vh; overflow: auto; padding: 18px; border: 1px solid var(--linie-stark); border-radius: 8px; color: var(--tinte); background: var(--papier); }
+.zyklus-bestaetigung-dialog h2 { margin-block-start: 0; font-size: 1.2em; }
+.zyklus-bestaetigung-dialog .dialog-knoepfe { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
diff --git a/magnolie-organizer-windows/shared/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js b/magnolie-organizer-windows/shared/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js
index b388893104c02d160e13744643618c88b24b25d2..fbc93684fba177a8c83090c6bdf237f8046da3b1 100644
--- a/magnolie-organizer-windows/shared/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js
+++ b/magnolie-organizer-windows/shared/magnolie-handbuch/web/i18n-markers.js
@@ -37,7 +37,6 @@ gettext("<h3>Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h3><div class='achtung'><b>
 gettext("<h3>Drawing sheets and signatures</h3><p>Enable the custom tab, open Customize, and add a Drawing sheet. Draw with mouse, touch or pen; choose color and width, erase, undo or redo. Changes are saved automatically. Export PNG creates an image; Drawing sheet in the note editor embeds a PNG copy.</p><p>Complete backups and full recovery restore the editable original. Drawing modules are excluded from Custom task/appointment synchronization; an image deliberately embedded in a note follows that note’s sharing permissions.</p><p>For built-in KDE Connect tablet input, enable it on the sheet, then open the drawing tablet on the paired phone. Pen pressure and eraser events are supported. Leaving the sheet, locking or changing the source ends input. System KDE Connect can provide ordinary pen events where its tablet plugin is supported.</p><h3>Dynamic drawing sheet and symbol tools</h3><p>Magnolie symbols stay in at most two toolbar rows, named by tooltips. Right-click for variants: pen/nib/brush/highlighter, move view/move selection, fill/gradient and shapes. The nib angle is adjustable; its default makes horizontal strokes thin and vertical strokes thick. The pressure-sensitive brush tapers at both ends.</p><p>The automatic drawing surface dynamically fills the available field and adapts to window size. The earlier 1500 × 1300 dimensions were an example, not a fixed sheet format. Existing strokes and pictures retain their proportions; extra drawing space is added as needed. Zoom affects the drawing view, not its toolbar. Sheet size can explicitly select a fixed format or return to Automatic.</p><p><b>Open</b> loads pictures or SVG drawings for additions such as a signature. The original appearance stays as an image background; new strokes remain editable. Magnolie JSON loads stored editable strokes. The broom clears the sheet; the trash symbol removes the sheet to the recycle bin. New creates another sheet and the selector switches between them. Selection, cut/paste, fill/gradient, shapes, rotation and undo/redo use the existing drawing logic.</p><p>An available paired KDE Connect tablet source automatically binds to the active drawing surface. Open the drawing tablet on the phone; no separate sheet activation is needed. Directly connected pens and mouse use the same surface. Sheet/window changes, locking and disconnection end the old input context.</p><p><b>Save as</b> opens one file dialog for PNG, SVG or editable Magnolie JSON and its location. Print remains in the bottom print selection. Note editor → Drawing sheet lets you edit existing sheets or create new ones and embed a PNG attachment.</p><p>Readable sheet selection and line width sit at the left, with ordered document actions and drawing tools at the right. Narrow book fields stack these areas and adapt the drawing surface to the remaining space. Open also supports JPG and scanned PDFs. For a multi-page PDF, select the page to use as the image background for additions or a signature; the original PDF file is not modified. Without selected strokes, Rotate turns the entire sheet, background and editable strokes together; with a selection it turns only the selected elements. Undo and redo retain the complete sheet state. Closing the last open sheet creates a new blank sheet while keeping the previous drawing stored and selectable again.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>Edit</h3><p>Click an appointment in the month overview, week view, or day view. The appointment sheet opens over the book and displays all its details. Make your changes, then click <span class='knopfwort'>Edit appointment</span> at the bottom right. Press <kbd>Esc</kbd> to close the sheet without making changes.</p><h3>Delete</h3><p>Open the appointment and click <span class='knopfwort'>Delete</span> at the bottom left. A confirmation prompt appears over the appointment sheet. Click <span class='knopfwort'>Delete</span> again to confirm.</p><div class='merke'><b>Nothing disappears immediately</b>Deleted items first go to the <b>Recycle bin</b>, from which you can recover them if the recycle bin is enabled. See page <b data-page='the-recycle-bin' class='knopfwort'></b> for instructions.</div><h3>Reschedule an appointment</h3><p>You cannot drag an appointment to another day with the mouse. Open it and change <b>Date</b> and, if necessary, <b>Through</b>. Then click <span class='knopfwort'>Edit appointment</span> to apply the change.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>Enable once, then select the notes</h3><p>Sending is off by default. Under Settings → General → Send notes by email or fax, enable Show Send in note print options. In Notes, open Selection options, tick the required notes and click the single Send button. Choose an available Email or Fax route, select a contact address or enter a recipient manually, enter the subject and click Send.</p><p>The PDF contains exactly the selected text printout. Embedded images and PDF attachments are not included. Print now opens printing only and never sends. Email opens the supported mail client's compose flow; complete the message there. Fax hands the document directly to the configured server queue.</p><h3>Available routes and the result</h3><p>Linux email needs a registered supported mail client and xdg-email. Fax needs a configured HylaFAX server and installed sendfax. Windows email needs a registered compatible Simple-MAPI client; no Windows fax adapter is provided. The email attachment route is unavailable in Flatpak. Only available routes are offered.</p><p>Cancel sending prevents handoff before external dispatch. Closing the progress window does not recall an already started handoff. A handoff is not delivery confirmation; check the external application or fax server. Prepared PDFs use a private cache and are cleaned on the next use after one day. Your original notes remain unchanged.</p><p>Selection options also offers Fax without an installed adapter: choose Fax printer, Network fax server or Online fax service. Printing uses the system fax printer. Online service creates the selected PDF and opens an HTTPS portal for manual upload. Only a configured supported server can send directly; opening the choices sends nothing.</p>");
-gettext("<h3>Estimated next period</h3><p>Notifications are off unless enabled below.</p><ul><li>Estimate the next period</li><li>Report unusual cycle intervals</li></ul><p>At least three recorded starts are needed. Bleeding days up to three days apart form one episode; only intervals of 14–60 days enter the median.</p><p><b>Difference (days): 7</b></p>");
 gettext("<h3>Explicitly share a note</h3><p>Open the note you want and select <span class='knopfwort'>Share together</span>. The note becomes shared only after you confirm the security prompt and the other party accepts the transfer. Subsequent changes to the heading, text, embedded images and PDF files are transmitted in both directions.</p><p>The other party receives a system notification and sees the number and total size of the attachments. With <b>Accept and remember</b>, consent remains in effect, but only for this note and this confirmed branch. Further changes then arrive automatically.</p><div class='merke'><b>Only this note</b>Other notebooks and pages remain private. A size limit applies to the attachments transferred together; if they exceed it, the Organizer tells you before sending them.</div><h3>Working with a small group</h3><p>If several confirmed branches are connected, <b>Workgroup (all)</b> appears when you share an entry. This lets you send the same appointment, contact or note to every member. Each member must still accept new offers individually.</p><div class='achtung'><b>A changed key is detected</b>The key of a confirmed branch cannot be replaced without your knowledge. Deliberately remove the old connection, and compare a new fingerprint especially carefully.</div>");
 gettext("<h3>Exporting selected Contacts to ODS</h3><p>Only in Contacts, an <span class='knopfwort'>ODS</span> button exports the checked contacts to a spreadsheet. The column choices below the contact list are initially collapsed; open them to select the desired columns in one vertical list. The export honors first-name or last-name ordering. The primary street and house number, postal code and city, landline, mobile number and email addresses have separate columns without repeated standard labels. Further addresses and phone numbers remain in dedicated additional columns. Further phone numbers appear one per line without labels. Birthdays are included even when an imported anniversary is linked by name only. Emergency contacts and notes remain available as well. The file embeds the Magnolie logo and is configured as an A4 landscape table.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>Finding anything again</h3><p>The wide <b>Search</b> field searches groups, notebooks, page titles, written text, and the names of embedded files. Clear it to display all pages again.</p><h3>Arranging things your way</h3><p><span class='knopfwort'>Customize</span> opens the notebook manager. There you can move groups and notebooks with the arrow buttons, sort them alphabetically, or move a notebook to another group.</p><h3>Links, images, and PDF files</h3><p>Above the writing area are buttons for adding a web or email link, an image, or a PDF file. Once selected, the item is securely embedded in the note, so the original file can then be moved. Each image or PDF file can be up to 8 MiB. Drag the dotted divider handle above the attachments down to see more of the note text, or up to enlarge the previews. In a small window or with a shallow attachment area, images and PDF files automatically appear as compact icons.</p><div class='merke'><b>Included in a complete backup</b>Your notes, their organization, and their attachments are all included in the data backup. There is no separate option for exporting notes under <i>Export</i>. Printed notes include their titles and text, but not embedded images or PDF pages.</div>");
@@ -61,6 +60,7 @@ gettext("<h3>Navigation and recording</h3><p>Settings lists Version, Connections
 gettext("<h3>New and already present</h3><p>After a file or folder import, Magnolie Notes reports how many notes were taken over and how many were already present. A duplicate is recognized from the normalized <b>title and text</b>. Filename, source, notebook and date do not distinguish it, so the same wording from another source is skipped as already present. Notes already stored without an import identity are not compared retroactively.</p><h3>Where the notes go</h3><p>Keep uses its first label or the notebook <b>Google Keep</b>. Evernote, Simplenote and Standard Notes use a notebook carrying their product name. Plain files use a recognized source or <b>Imported</b>. Existing notebook names are reused; directory names do not create a notebook hierarchy.</p><h3>ZIP safety limits</h3><p>A ZIP may contain at most <b>5,000 entries</b>, with at most <b>8 MiB</b> uncompressed per entry and <b>64 MiB</b> uncompressed altogether. Nested and multipart ZIP files are not read. A damaged archive or a violated ZIP limit rejects the complete archive instead of importing an uncertain partial result.</p><h3>When nothing arrives</h3><p><i>No readable notes were found in this file.</i> means that no nonblank title or text was produced. <i>The import failed.</i> also covers malformed or oversized ZIP files. A repeated direct share may use the first wording instead of explicitly saying that the note was a duplicate.</p><div class='achtung'><b>Keep the export until you have checked it</b>Open several imported notes, inspect notebooks, check-list marks and dates, and compare the reported number. Only then remove the original export.</div>");
 gettext("<h3>Nextcloud</h3><p>A server platform that Magnolie can use for CalDAV and CardDAV synchronization and for a separate WebDAV mailbox.</p><h3>Notification</h3><p>A message shown by the operating system, for example for a due reminder, an incoming call, or permitted Android app information.</p><h3>Pairing</h3><p>The deliberate association of two devices or branches, including identity checks and the permissions granted to that partner.</p><h3>PDF</h3><p>A fixed-layout document format used by Magnolie for print output and supported note attachments.</p><h3>Personal Sync</h3><p>Synchronization of notes, notebooks, and own tasks between one person's desktop and one phone marked as an own device; it excludes calendars, contacts, and shared Magnolienbaum entries.</p><h3>Port</h3><p>A numbered TCP or UDP endpoint through which a network service receives traffic, such as TCP 8741 for the Magnolie phone connection.</p><h3>Recovery snapshot</h3><p>An integrity-checked short-term copy of the complete main-data set inside Magnolie's data location; it is not a backup against disk or device loss.</p><h3>Recycle bin</h3><p>Local retention for supported deleted Organizer items, from which they can be restored until they expire or are removed permanently.</p><h3>RFCOMM</h3><p>A Bluetooth serial-data transport used as a permitted manual fallback for the Magnolie phone protocol; it uses no IP firewall port.</p><h3>SHA-256</h3><p>A cryptographic hash function used for file checksums, attachment identities, and other integrity checks.</p><h3>SMS</h3><p>A mobile-network text message. In Magnolie Organizer, reading and sending SMS uses KDE Connect rather than Magnolie Notes or Personal Sync.</p><h3>Synchronization</h3><p>The controlled comparison and exchange of changes between stores, with Magnolie-specific conflict, permission, and deletion safeguards.</p><h3>Time zone</h3><p>A regional rule set such as <b>Europe/Berlin</b> that relates local dates and times to absolute instants.</p><h3>TLS</h3><p>Transport Layer Security, which encrypts a network connection and authenticates its peer by certificate; KDE Connect uses mutually authenticated TLS.</p><h3>Tray</h3><p>The desktop notification area beside the clock, where Magnolie can remain available while its main window is hidden.</p><h3>UFW</h3><p>Uncomplicated Firewall, a Linux firewall frontend for which the Debian package supplies an optional Magnolie application profile.</p><h3>URI</h3><p>A standardized resource identifier, including addresses such as <b>https:</b> links and <b>sms:</b> recipients.</p><h3>vCard</h3><p>A standard contact exchange format, usually stored in a <b>.vcf</b> file and supported by Magnolie import and export.</p><h3>VPN</h3><p>A virtual private network that can securely connect devices or networks over another network; Magnolie does not create one automatically.</p><h3>Wayland</h3><p>A modern Linux display protocol under which the compositor controls details such as exact window placement.</p><h3>WebDAV</h3><p>HTTP-based access to remote files and collections; Magnolie uses a Nextcloud WebDAV folder as an optional message mailbox.</p><h3>Wi-Fi</h3><p>A wireless IP network and the preferred transport for Magnolie phone connections and Personal Sync.</p><h3>X11</h3><p>The traditional Linux window-system protocol, under which Magnolie can restore an exact window position where the window manager permits it.</p><h3>XDG</h3><p>Freedesktop.org conventions and environment variables that define standard Linux locations for data, configuration, and state files.</p><h3>ZIP</h3><p>A compressed archive format accepted by selected Magnolie imports under strict entry, size, path, and compression-ratio limits.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>People responsible</h3><p>Use <span class='knopfwort'>People</span> to add, rename, or remove people. On the task form, you can select one or more people. Colored initials beside the task then show who is responsible.</p><h3>Filter the list</h3><p>Above the task list, you can select a person and a date range if required. <span class='knopfwort'>Clear selection</span> displays everything again. The printed output uses exactly the same people and date filters.</p><h3>Set a reminder for the due date</h3><p>When creating or editing a task, select <b>remind me on the due date</b>. The reminder appears in the morning and also names the people responsible. Reminders must be enabled globally for this to work.</p><p>Under <b>Custom notification</b>, you can also choose a lead time of one to seven days. The field starts blank and displays the gray hint <i>e.g. 1 day before</i>. You can use the due-date reminder and the custom lead time either together or separately.</p><div class='merke'><b>A task for an appointment</b>On the appointment sheet, you can link an existing task or create a new one. You can also give the new task its own reminder there.</div><div class='achtung'><b>When exporting</b>A task export includes the title, due date, priority, status, and note. People, reminders, and appointment links are retained only in a complete backup.</div>");
+gettext("<h3>Period forecast (estimate)</h3><p>Calendar display and reminders can be enabled separately. Existing entries are preserved.</p><p>Notifications are off unless enabled below.</p><ul><li>☐ Show period forecast in calendar</li><li>☐ Notify before the estimated period</li><li>☐ Report unusual cycle intervals</li></ul><p><b>Difference (days): 7</b></p><p><b>💧 ≈</b> Pale drops mark possible start days, not a predicted bleeding duration. Active predictions disappear after the estimated window if unconfirmed. Only days you confirm as actual bleeding enter future calculations. Click a drop for today or an earlier day and explicitly select the bleeding intensity actually observed. Confirmation records only that day and recalculates the estimate. Future days cannot be confirmed; Cancel leaves your records unchanged.</p><p>When hints are enabled, a separate pale dashed drop may appear at the earlier estimated start after the forecast expires. Its tooltip only says that no new start is recorded; it does not prove a missed period. Dashed drops can also explain changes or uncertainty in recorded intervals and bleeding. They never count as entries.</p><h3>Details and limitations</h3><p>Calculated from at least three starts. Bleeding entries up to three days apart form one episode. After an interval outside 14–60 days, two new intervals are needed. The window spans the shortest and longest of up to twelve recent intervals, plus two days on either side.</p><p>Estimate from your entries, not a diagnosis or contraception method. Seek medical advice for new, persistent or distressing changes.</p><h3>Pause forecasts</h3><p>Click a dashed drop and choose pregnancy, breastfeeding, medication/hormonal treatment, perimenopause/menopause, or another reason. Pregnancy initially suggests nine calendar months from recording the pause; this is not a due date. Other reasons initially have no fixed end. For every reason you can change the end date or leave it open.</p><p>The pause includes its final day; without a date it remains until explicitly ended. Forecasts, missing-start hints and cycle reminders stop, while a neutral status shows the reason and end. New observed bleeding is saved, but the pause ends only if you separately confirm it as a new period. Keep pause or cancelling that question preserves both the bleeding record and the pause. Ending the pause manually resumes planning today without creating a bleeding entry.</p><p>After resumption, only entries from the resumption day, or after the scheduled end, form the new history. Three new starts are needed; old cycles do not produce an overdue warning. Confirm bleeding as a new period only if that is how it has been identified. Bleeding during pregnancy needs prompt medical advice; bleeding after menopause also needs medical assessment. Ending a planning pause does not establish that a pregnancy or menopause has ended.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>Phone contacts (KDE Connect)</h3><p>Pair the phone in KDE Connect and allow contact access there. Open <b>Settings ▸ Synchronization ▸ Phone contacts (KDE Connect)</b> and choose <b>Import preview</b>. No Google or Microsoft account and no photo retrieval are required.</p><p>Review new contacts, the existing target and differing fields. Ambiguous matches wait for your choice. Apply saves in Organizer after a recovery snapshot; Cancel changes nothing. Repeating does not create duplicate contacts. Local changes and manually selected or removed photos are retained. Missing contacts never cause deletion. Nothing is written back to the phone. System KDE uses its synchronized contact cache.</p><h3>Google on Linux: step by step</h3><ol class='schritte'><li><b>Mint/Cinnamon:</b> open the application menu, search for <b>Online Accounts</b> and open it. Select <b>Google</b> from the providers.</li><li><b>Ubuntu/GNOME:</b> open Activities, search for <b>Online Accounts</b> and open the Settings panel. Under <b>Connect an Account</b>, select <b>Google</b>.</li><li>Follow Google's sign-in window or browser page and review the requested access. Afterwards, enable the offered <b>Calendar</b> and <b>Contacts</b> services you want to use. First check that your calendars and address books appear in the corresponding system applications.</li></ol><h3>TUXEDO/KDE</h3><ol class='schritte'><li>Open <b>System Settings ▸ Online Accounts ▸ Add New Account… ▸ Google</b>. Follow the provider's sign-in flow.</li><li>The online account alone does not prove that an Akonadi calendar or address book exists. For the KDE connection, install Magnolie's matching KDE component and the system packages <b>akonadi-server</b> and <b>kdepim-runtime</b>. KAddressBook and KOrganizer provide the address-book and calendar interfaces.</li><li>If no suitable Google resource exists, open <b>KAddressBook ▸ File ▸ New ▸ Add Address Book…</b>, select <b>Google Groupware</b> and confirm with <b>OK</b>. Complete its account setup and check the calendars and address books it provides. Use an existing suitable resource rather than adding the same account again.</li></ol><h3>Select sources in Magnolie</h3><p>Open <b>Settings ▸ Synchronization</b>, select the desired calendars and address book, then choose <b>Synchronize now</b>. A system login, a calendar, an address book and a contact photo are separate things: photos are available only when the selected source actually supplies them. Google Tasks is a separate integration and is not enabled by these steps. Labels may vary with the installed desktop version.</p>");
 gettext("<h3>Samsung and Play Protect, step by step</h3><p>The release APK is signed with the Magnolie production certificate, but it is distributed outside Google Play. It therefore has no Google Play Store or Play Protect developer certification. Samsung and Google may show a general warning because they do not know this distribution source or developer through the store. This warning does not by itself prove that the file is malicious, but the signature does not replace checking its official origin and SHA-256 checksum.</p><div class='abbildungsreihe'><figure><img src='01.jpg' alt='Samsung warning that the downloaded file may be harmful'><figcaption>1. After checking the source and SHA-256 value, choose <b>Open file</b>.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src='02.jpg' alt='Google Play Protect blocks Magnolie Notes and offers Further details'><figcaption>2. Expand <b>Further details</b>; do not disable Play Protect globally.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src='03.jpg' alt='Expanded Play Protect dialog with Install anyway'><figcaption>3. Choose <b>Install anyway</b> only for the verified official APK.</figcaption></figure></div><div class='achtung'><b>The exact wording can differ</b>Android, Samsung One UI and Play Protect change these dialogs between versions. Stop if the app name, source, certificate expectations or checksum do not match the official release.</div>");
 gettext("<h3>Select contact cards</h3><p>Open <span class='knopfwort'>Selection options</span> in the footer. All names appear on the left with a checkbox; the right side previews the selected cards. Use <span class='knopfwort'>All</span> and <span class='knopfwort'>None</span>, then choose <span class='knopfwort'>Print now</span>, <span class='knopfwort'>ODS</span>, or <span class='knopfwort'>Delete selection</span>.</p><p>Deleting requires confirmation. With the recycle bin enabled, the contacts go there; otherwise they are removed permanently. Derived anniversaries are removed as well, while linked appointments and tasks remain and are merely disconnected from the contacts.</p><h3>Merge duplicate contact cards</h3><p>Duplicates inevitably accumulate over the years: the same person may appear twice, once with a postal address and once with a phone number. Use <span class='knopfwort'>Merge duplicate contact cards</span> under <span class='knopfwort'>Settings ▸ Contacts</span> to resolve them.</p><p>The Organizer searches for matching names, email addresses, and phone numbers. Capitalization in email addresses is ignored; national phone numbers and the same numbers with a country code are treated as identical. The Organizer shows how many groups it found, provides examples, and asks for confirmation <b>twice</b> before making any changes.</p><p>When contacts are merged, the most complete card is retained and all email addresses, phone numbers, and postal addresses are combined. <i>Straße</i>, <i>Strasse</i>, and <i>Str.</i> are treated as equivalent. Notes are appended to one another. A copy of every removed card remains in the recycle bin under <i>Duplicates</i>.</p><div class='achtung'><b>Check the results</b>Take a moment to inspect several merged contact cards. If anything is incorrect, recover the copy from the recycle bin.</div>");
